"""Render seeded variants from native captures; retain yesterday's evidence."""
from pathlib import Path
import hashlib
import json
import shutil
import markdown

ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[4]
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
RUN=ROOT/'ada_run/encounter_pilot/Random_Entropy/seeded-hybrids'
for name in ['report.json','hall-full.png','hall-seed-436.png','source_manifest.json']:
    shutil.copy2(RUN/name,HERE/('museum-report.json' if name=='report.json' else name))
reports=[json.loads((HERE/name).read_text(encoding='utf8')) for name in ['verification.json','museum-report.json']]
assert all(report['passed'] for report in reports)
counts=[len(report['checks']) for report in reports]
wall=json.loads((ROOT/'commons/maps/Random_Entropy/writing_wall.json').read_text(encoding='utf8'))
assert wall['order'][:6]==['shannon_entropy_meter','entropy_jar','entropy_compartments','entropy_axiom','entropy_ruin','signal_room']
style='''body{margin:0;background:#f1eee5;color:#233b39;font:18px/1.55 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1400px;margin:auto;padding:24px}h1{font:clamp(30px,4vw,46px)/1.1 Georgia,serif;margin:10px 0 16px}h2{font:28px Georgia,serif}p{max-width:85ch}small{letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5d736c}a{color:#166965}nav{display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap}section{margin:28px 0}figure{margin:0}img{display:block;width:100%;max-height:70vh;object-fit:contain;background:#101d25}figcaption{padding:12px;background:#e0e5d9}label{display:inline-block;padding:12px 22px 12px 3px;cursor:pointer}input{accent-color:#1b736b}.variant{display:none}#s435:checked~.views .s435,#s436:checked~.views .s436,#s437:checked~.views .s437,#s438:checked~.views .s438{display:block}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:18px}.grid img{max-height:none}code{font-size:.9em}td,th{padding:10px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #aebfb3}table{border-collapse:collapse}pre{overflow:auto}@media(max-width:850px){.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}'''
photos={435:'hybrid-detail.png',436:'seed-436-detail.png',437:'seed-437-detail.png',438:'seed-438-detail.png'}
controls=''.join(f'<input type="radio" name="seed" id="s{seed}" '+('checked' if seed==435 else '')+f'><label for="s{seed}">Seed {seed}</label>' for seed in photos)
views=''.join(f'<figure class="variant s{seed}"><img src="{photo}" alt="Four hybrids generated from seed {seed}"><figcaption>Seed {seed} · same fifty meshes and materials, different memberships and joins. Native Godot capture at HYBRIDS (1).</figcaption></figure>' for seed,photo in photos.items())
page=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Different seeds, different hybrids · Ada Research</title><style>{style}</style><main>
<header><small>Ada Research / Random_Entropy / 16 October 2026</small><h1>Different seeds, different hybrids</h1><p>The seed now changes which parts come together, their joining order, attachment faces and turns. The four display pads remain; the forms on them vary. KEEP preserves an interesting arrangement, and REPLAY brings it back exactly.</p>
<nav><a href="#compare">Side by side</a><a href="#try">Try the loop</a><a href="guide.html">Reconstruction guide</a><a href="/book-review/commons/maps/Random_Entropy/tutorial.md">Updated tutorial</a></nav></header>
<section role="group" aria-label="Seed comparison">{controls}<div class="views">{views}</div></section>
<section id="compare"><h2>A part can enter another relationship</h2><div class="grid"><figure><img src="hybrid-detail.png" alt="Seed 435 assemblies"><figcaption>435 · trace a recognisable part.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="seed-436-detail.png" alt="Seed 436 assemblies"><figcaption>436 · find what now carries it, or what it carries.</figcaption></figure></div><p>Small bundles stay intact: the screen keeps its bezel, the stool base keeps its feet. The seed moves these bundles between hybrids and changes how they join. Each new form has at least three source donors, named on its label.</p></section>
<section id="try"><h2>Keep a form while exploring others</h2><ol><li>In the Entropy hall, near the entrance at grid (13, 3), select HYBRIDS.</li><li>Press SEED +1. Hold stage and viewpoint fixed while comparing the new forms.</li><li>Press KEEP when a relationship is worth returning to.</li><li>Try more seeds or move back through separated parts to original objects.</li><li>Press REPLAY to recover the kept seed, stage, memberships and exact part poses—even after reopening the scene.</li></ol><p>The standalone <code>commons/artifacts/prefab_disorder/preview.tscn</code> has the same controls. KEEP also works between stages. Earlier separation records and yesterday's four fixed hybrids remain replayable.</p></section>
<section><h2>The installed room</h2><figure><img src="hall-seed-436.png" alt="Seed 436 generated by the physical seed button in the Entropy hall"><figcaption>The room test presses SEED +1, verifies a new assembly, then replays the previously kept form.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section><h2>What is established</h2><p><strong>{counts[0]} apparatus checks and {counts[1]} room checks pass.</strong> Thirty-nine sampled seeds produce thirty-nine different membership sets, even when pad permutations are ignored. All fifty parts remain, every hybrid has multiple donors, slider reversal retraces its poses, and fresh scenes reconstruct saved forms exactly.</p><p>The joining grammar is authored and uses bounding faces. It is not a physical joint solver or an entropy measurement. Whether a particular form becomes interesting, recognisable or suggestive of a new use remains a human research question; headset comfort is still untested.</p>
<nav><a href="verification.json">Apparatus evidence</a><a href="museum-report.json">Room evidence</a><a href="kept-trial.json">Saved seed 435</a><a href="seed-436.json">Seed 436 record</a><a href="manifest.json">Source fingerprints</a><a href="../2026-10-15-prefab-hybrids/index.html">Yesterday's fixed hybrids</a></nav></section></main></html>'''
(HERE/'index.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf8')
guide=(ROOT/'commons/artifacts/prefab_disorder/README.md').read_text(encoding='utf8')
(HERE/'implementation.md').write_text(guide,encoding='utf8')
guide=guide.replace('../../../doc/book/iterations/2026-10-16-seeded-hybrids/README.md','index.html')
(HERE/'guide.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Seeded hybrid reconstruction</title><style>'+style+'</style><main><a href="index.html">← Seed comparison</a>'+markdown.markdown(guide,extensions=['tables','fenced_code'])+'</main></html>',encoding='utf8')
paths=list((ROOT/'commons/artifacts/prefab_disorder').glob('*.gd'))+list((ROOT/'commons/artifacts/prefab_disorder').glob('*.tscn'))
paths+=[ROOT/'commons/artifacts/registry/prefab_disorder.json']
paths+=[ROOT/'commons/maps/Random_Entropy'/name for name in ['map_data.json','writing_wall.json','tutorial.md','final.md','artifacts.md']]
for source in ['cardboard_box','computer_monitor','lab_stool','microscope']:
    paths += [ROOT/'commons/artifacts'/source/(source+suffix) for suffix in ['.gd','.tscn']]
(HERE/'manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps({'checks':counts,'generator':'seeded-grafts/2','sampled_seeds':reports[0]['sampled_seeds'],'distinct_memberships':reports[0]['distinct_memberships'],'main_order':wall['order'][:6],'sha256':{p.relative_to(ROOT).as_posix():hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in paths}},indent=2),encoding='utf8')
(HERE/'README.md').write_text(f'''# Seeded hybrids

16 October 2026. User asks for seeds to change the forms themselves while KEEP/REPLAY retains interesting results.

[Native visual comparison](index.html) · [Guide](implementation.md) · [Apparatus checks](verification.json) · [Actual hall checks](museum-report.json) · [Kept seed 435](kept-trial.json) · [Seed 436](seed-436.json) · [Source manifest](manifest.json).

`seeded_grafts.gd` distributes fifteen recognisable bundles across four display pads, then varies joining order, attachment faces, small offsets and quarter turns. All fifty original meshes remain. Each hybrid receives at least three source objects. The grammar fits each finished assembly uniformly to its pad. This is a geometric assembly procedure, not physical self-assembly.

{counts[0]}/{counts[0]} native apparatus checks and {counts[1]}/{counts[1]} actual-hall checks pass. Thirty-nine sampled seeds (including negative and int64 boundary values) produce thirty-nine distinct membership sets after ignoring pad permutations. Checks cover deterministic reconstruction, complete bounded mixed-source inventory, seed-wrap behavior, intermediate reversal, original geometry/materials, fresh saved replay and invalid-record rejection. Historical separation-only records and previous fixed-hybrid records retain their old geometry and recipe identity. SEED +1 after an old replay explicitly switches to the new generator.

The suite initially found two test-fixture issues: canonical membership comparison needed to normalize JSON numeric item IDs to integers; the invalid-scale case needed to zero a whole basis column rather than a component that can already be zero after a quarter turn. Both were corrected before recording the passing receipt. No generator or replay check was weakened.

Reproduce apparatus evidence with `python -X utf8 doc/book/iterations/2026-10-16-seeded-hybrids/run.py`. Reproduce room evidence with `python -X utf8 tools/run_encounter_probe.py Random_Entropy --sequence randomness --render --no-bridges --output-tag seeded-hybrids --probe doc/book/iterations/2026-10-16-seeded-hybrids/museum_probe.gd`. Run `publish.py` here after both pass.

The artifact guide, optional map tutorial/writing-wall entry, registry and research card/plan now describe seeded recombination. The six-stop main room/final order and first 48-value research pilot remain in place. Human recognition, independent learner reconstruction and headset comfort remain untested. Next: preserve two seeds at the same stage and compare a part's apparent role or use; a later controlled rule change should retain the separated baseline.
''',encoding='utf8')
print('Published',HERE/'index.html',counts)
